From: OneEmu build <Manggome@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] citra_libretro: expose "disable right eye rendering" as a core option

Azahar's renderer can skip the top screen's right-eye image
(Settings::values.disable_right_eye_render, video_core/right_eye_disabler.cpp);
its Qt and Android frontends offer it as "Disable Right Eye Rendering"
("Greatly improves performance in some games"). The libretro frontend never
reads or sets it, so the libretro core always draws both eyes even though it
has no stereoscopic output at all (render_3d is never set, stays Off) and the
second image is thrown away.

Add citra_disable_right_eye_render (graphics category, default enabled) and
feed it into the setting. RightEyeDisabler re-reads the setting at every frame
end, so changing the option in-game takes effect without a restart. Titles that
break with it (Luigi's Mansion 1/2, Rayman Origins) are already excluded by the
core's own hack list (common/hacks/hack_list.cpp, HackType::RIGHT_EYE_DISABLE,
applied per title in GSP_GPU::AcquireGpuRight via RightEyeDisabler::SetEnabled),
whatever the option says.

diff --git a/src/citra_libretro/core_settings.cpp b/src/citra_libretro/core_settings.cpp
index 085f7ac..b360b22 100644
--- a/src/citra_libretro/core_settings.cpp
+++ b/src/citra_libretro/core_settings.cpp
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@ static constexpr const char* texture_filter = citra_setting(BaseKeys::texture_fi
 static constexpr const char* texture_sampling = citra_setting(BaseKeys::texture_sampling);
 static constexpr const char* custom_textures = citra_setting(BaseKeys::custom_textures);
 static constexpr const char* dump_textures = citra_setting(BaseKeys::dump_textures);
+static constexpr const char* disable_right_eye_render =
+    citra_setting(BaseKeys::disable_right_eye_render);
 } // namespace graphics

 namespace layout {
@@ -440,6 +442,22 @@ static constexpr retro_core_option_v2_definition option_definitions[] = {
         },
         config::disabled
     },
+    {
+        config::graphics::disable_right_eye_render,
+        "Disable Right Eye Rendering",
+        "Disable Right Eye Rendering",
+        "Skip drawing the right-eye image of the top screen. The libretro core never shows "
+        "stereoscopic 3D, so that image is wasted work. Greatly improves performance in some "
+        "games; titles known to flicker with it are excluded automatically.",
+        nullptr,
+        config::category::graphics,
+        {
+            { config::enabled, "Enabled" },
+            { config::disabled, "Disabled" },
+            { nullptr, nullptr }
+        },
+        config::enabled
+    },

     // Layout Category
     {
@@ -936,6 +954,10 @@ static void ParseGraphicsOptions(void) {

     Settings::values.dump_textures = LibRetro::FetchVariable(config::graphics::dump_textures,
                                                              config::disabled) == config::enabled;
+
+    Settings::values.disable_right_eye_render =
+        LibRetro::FetchVariable(config::graphics::disable_right_eye_render, config::enabled) ==
+        config::enabled;
 }

 static Settings::LayoutOption GetLayoutOption(const std::string& name) {
